(D5 — Discrepancy 5 repro: old manual line 2753 says "the first append
 determines the list's element type for printing". It does not: each
 element renders by its own runtime tag regardless of what was appended
 first, in both directions. The rendering rule twenty lines earlier
 (LANGUAGE.md:2782-2784) is the one the compiler follows.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D5.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   ["text first", 42]
   [42, "then text"]
)
a list called sayings is [].
append "text first" to sayings.
append 42 to sayings.
print sayings.

a list called tallies is [].
append 42 to tallies.
append "then text" to tallies.
